                <h2>1. Account Balance Alert Mechanism</h2>
<p>Empty ad account balance is the #1 cause of campaign interruptions. Operations teams should establish a three-tier alert system:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Yellow Alert</strong>: Balance below 2x daily spend, notify recharge responsible person 48 hours in advance</li>
<li><strong>Orange Alert</strong>: Balance below 1x daily spend, trigger expedited financial approval process</li>
<li><strong>Red Alert</strong>: Balance below 0.5x daily spend, immediately pause non-core campaigns and initiate emergency recharge</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Checklist</strong>:<br />
- [ ] Confirm balance monitoring tools are functioning properly<br />
- [ ] Verify alert notifications reach responsible parties via both email and SMS<br />
- [ ] Record recent downtime caused by insufficient balance</p>
<h2>2. Recharge Rhythm Planning</h2>
<p>Blind recharging and emergency recharging both cause capital efficiency loss. Plan according to these rhythms:</p>
<p><strong>Short-cycle accounts (TikTok, Google Ads)</strong>: Fixed weekly recharge day, maintain balance covering 7-10 days of spend</p>
<p><strong>Long-cycle accounts (Meta, Pinterest)</strong>: Evaluate bi-weekly, adjust recharge amount based on campaign schedule</p>
<p><strong>Execution Steps</strong>:<br />
1. Export spend reports from all platforms on the first day of each cycle<br />
2. Calculate average daily spend rate over the past 4 weeks<br />
3. Forecast next 2 weeks spend based on schedule<br />
4. Submit recharge application with estimated depletion date</p>
<h2>3. Spend Velocity Monitoring</h2>
<p>Spend variation across campaigns in the same account can exceed 5x. Operations must verify weekly:</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Anomaly Type</th>
<th>Criteria</th>
<th>Action</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Sudden Drop</td>
<td>Daily spend below 60% of average</td>
<td>Check for budget cap or audit triggers</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Sudden Spike</td>
<td>Daily spend exceeds 150% of average</td>
<td>Immediately investigate creative breakout or fraudulent traffic</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Zero Spend</td>
<td>Campaign live but no spend</td>
<td>Verify bidding, audience, or account status</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<h2>4. Multi-Account Fund Health Assessment</h2>
<p>When managing 5+ accounts, conduct weekly horizontal comparison:</p>
<p><strong>Checklist</strong>:<br />
- [ ] Calculate each account's weekly spend as percentage of total budget<br />
- [ ] Identify accounts with spend below 5% or above 40%<br />
- [ ] Evaluate if any accounts are throttled due to insufficient balance<br />
- [ ] Record frequency and amount of inter-account fund transfers</p>
<h2>5. Financial Reconciliation SOP</h2>
<p>Month-end reconciliation is the closing action of fund management. Standard process:</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Export statements</strong>: Download current period statements from each platform (note timezone and billing cycle differences)</li>
<li><strong>Cross-verify</strong>: Compare platform statements with internal recharge records and spend reports</li>
<li><strong>Difference investigation</strong>: Trace causes for discrepancies over 1% (exchange rate fluctuations, tax deductions)</li>
<li><strong>Generate ledger</strong>: Complete "Monthly Ad Fund Ledger," with dual confirmation from finance and operations</li>
<li><strong>Archive for reference</strong>: Retain statements and reconciliation records for at least 12 months</li>
</ol>
<h2>6. Risk Control Checklist</h2>
<p>Risks in fund management hide in details. Complete monthly risk control checks:</p>
<p><strong>Account Level</strong>:<br />
- [ ] Confirm no abnormal IP access to accounts<br />
- [ ] Check billing address on linked cards/payment methods<br />
- [ ] Verify account permission assignments follow least privilege principle</p>
<p><strong>Fund Level</strong>:<br />
- [ ] Reconcile actual difference between prepaid recharges and spend<br />
- [ ] Check for long-term unspent account balances<br />
- [ ] Evaluate impact of exchange rate fluctuations on non-USD accounts</p>
<p><strong>Compliance Level</strong>:<br />
- [ ] Confirm each platform recharge channel complies with enterprise financial policies<br />
- [ ] Check if invoice acquisition matches recharge cycle<br />
- [ ] Retain complete audit trail of fund approval</p>
<hr />
<p><strong>Operations Tip</strong>: Print and post this checklist at workstations. Check off each completed item. If no alert-level events occur for 3 consecutive months, alert thresholds can be appropriately relaxed; if major anomalies occur, immediately initiate review and update check standards.</p>
